<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stavelot</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stavelot is a small town on the Amblève in the province of Liège, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>. It grew around the abbey founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/remaclus">Saint Remaclus</a> around 650, whose abbots ruled the ecclesiastical principality of Stavelot-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malmedy">Malmedy</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. The abbey was a centre of Mosan art, and the town is known today for its Laetare carnival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stavelot.jpg" alt="Stavelot" width="320" height="124" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Les Meloures at Luxembourgish Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stavelot.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
